2. Conditions

Exercise of the rights granted in Section 1 is expressly conditioned upon compliance with the following:

2.1. Source Code Disclosure Obligation: Any individual or entity that uses, reproduces, distributes, modifies, or aggregates files subject to COSPA must publicly disclose the complete and corresponding source code of all files covered by COSPA. Disclosure must be made via a publicly accessible channel without barriers to third-party access. No additional documentation or annotation is required beyond the source code itself.

2.2 License Integrity and Irrevocability
No person or entity, including the original Author, may actively modify, replace, or rescind the application of COSPA to any version of the Work that has been distributed or made publicly accessible. This License must remain in effect in its original form. You may not delete, alter, or obscure any terms or notices of this license.

2.3. Scope of Application: For any project referencing COSPA, all files within the project that do not hold an External License shall automatically be subject to COSPA pursuant to Section 0.4, and must strictly comply with all terms hereof, particularly Sections 2.1 and 2.2.

2.4. Collaborative Assent
The exercise of any right granted under this License shall constitute the user's express assent to have entered into a mutual collaborative agreement with the Copyright Holder regarding all terms of this License, and the user thereby agrees to be bound by such terms, including but not limited to the reciprocal source disclosure requirements set forth herein.

